{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And when you reap … for the poor and the stranger you shall leave them.</b> He explains that after we have accepted Him as Elohim, it is fitting for us to walk in His ways, to do righteousness and justice. Among the forms of charity are gleanings, forgotten sheaves, and the corner of the field, which are mentioned in this passage. This He explains by saying, אֲנִי ה׳ אֱלֹהֵיכֶם — that is, since I am your Elohim and all My ways are kindness and truth, it is fitting for you to observe these forms of charity that are desirable before Me."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:52.285234023Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}